            <ArticleTitle>Draft Genome Sequence of the Arsenic-Resistant Bacterium Brevundimonas denitrificans TAR-002T.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01326-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01326-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the 3.2-Mb draft genome sequence of Brevundimonas denitrificans strain TAR-002T, isolated from deep-sea floor sediment. The draft genome sequence of strain TAR-002T consists of 3,231,216 bp in 44 contigs, with a G+C content of 68.47%, 3,866 potential coding sequences (CDSs), 3 rRNAs, and 45 tRNAs.</AbstractText>
